Although I'm not a really good player myself, this is wat I'd do:

> 1) Should I visit the Mine's End and possibly Mine King first to try
> to round out my supplies even though I already almost certainly have a
> luckstone?

This is something I would rather do. First, this will allow you to be 
sure about the luck stone. Second, you will level up a bit, which will 
at the very least give you a few more hp. Third point is food.

> 2) Is there any chance I can fight the monsters that await me on DL 5?
> Or should I run past?  If it's the latter, it's very unlikely I'll be
> able to come back any time soon.  Since I haven't been able to buy any
> protection yet, this will make it difficult in the future.

I dunno if GDSM protects from stoning by asphinx, I'd look it up in some 
spoiler if I was you. Anyway, if I was you, I wouldn't even try to pick 
that fight yet.

> 3) What strategies should I use against the afforementioned nasties
> when I eventually face them?  What other equipiment should I look
> into?

The mines often give you a few useful wands. Try to gather a few wands 
of magic missile, striking, sleep and the like. Lightening would be 
perfect (though dangerous if found on a fast monster that doesn't go 
down in one hit).
Also, get telepathy (eat a floating eye corpse) and an uncursed 
blindfold/towel.
I'd rely on the good old strategy against stuff that's too powerful: Go 
down there blind (to see who is where with telepathy - be careful 
though, you won't see the stone golem that way, it has no brain, so 
unblind yourself first thing when you come down, after you know where 
the other nasties are). Then try to find the nasties seperated, but 
always be sure to have a clear way to an exit (really clear - a grid bug 
on the way is _not_ clear, it's calling for YASD). That's the hard part.
When you are so far, it gets pretty straight-forward: Stay at a good 
range from the monsters, zap, run away if they have come closer, rinse, 
repeat. Especially a wand of sleep combined with 
missile/striking/lightening/so on is wonderful for this strategy.

If in doubt, run away from the level.

> 4) Assuming that I remain above DL5 to prepare, how should I handle
> the food situation?  Relying on my god for food always makes me
> nervous.

Go grab yourself a tinning kit. If you can find one, it would help a lot.
Then get yourself some water (#dip useless potions into a fountain 2 
times), sacrifice a bit until you can safely pray, put the potions on 
the altar, stand on the altar yourself, pray. This will convert the 
water to holy water.
#dip your tinning kit into the holy water, thus getting a blessed 
tinning kit that makes blessed tins. Then go for the mines.
I personally prefer playing human vals exaclty because of this: The 
mines are a huge supply of food. As a dwarf, you are somewhat more 
restricted, but there's still plenty of food running around the mines. 
Plus let your pet finish off the friendlies. They tend to carry food.

I personally would rather pick another strategy though: Go down to level 
5, find a safe spot, dig down to level 6, and continue to sokoban. 
You'll find more food there than you can carry. Returning will be hard, 
but most likely, you'll also find a good collection of wands, allowing 
you to clear out lvl 5 pretty soon.

> 5) Is there anything else I should take into account that I haven't?

Uh... everything that I've forgotten to mention so far, which is surely 
a lot, should be taken into account too ;)

